# Goal 11: Fix lgamma / lgammaf — signgam not set

## Function
- `lgamma` (double precision)
- `lgammaf` (float precision)

## Source Files
- C (double): `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/lgammad.c`
- C (float): `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathf/lgammaf.c` and `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathf/internal/gammaf.c`
- Rust: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s3/src/lib.rs` (wrapper)

## Problem
MISMATCH: The function values match, but signgam is always 0 in Rust instead
of the correct value:
- C:    `lgamma 0x1p+0 = 0x0p+0 signgam 1`     Rust: `signgam 0`
- C:    `lgamma 0x1p+1 = 0x0p+0 signgam 1`     Rust: `signgam 0`
- C:    `lgamma 0x1p-1 = ... signgam 1`         Rust: `signgam 0`
- (7 more for lgamma, 6 for lgammaf — all have signgam 0 in Rust)

The Rust lgamma/lgammaf is not setting the global `signgam` variable.

## What Needs to Change
The Rust code must set the global `signgam` variable (an extern C int) to
match the C behavior. Compare how the C code sets signgam in lgammad.c and
lgammaf.c, and replicate in Rust. The bridge/test harness reads signgam
after calling lgamma, so it must be properly exported and written.

## Success Criteria
- All lgamma test cases return correct signgam values (1 or -1) matching C
- All lgammaf test cases return correct signgam values matching C
- Function return values remain correct
